scription":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518733,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg3MzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/usability","name":"usability","color":"447744","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-01-11T07:57:05Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T08:40:46Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.6.beta3.official [76dda5c6c]\n\n### System information\n\nw11\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen deleting a resource that is linked to multiple scenes, a confirmation window appears listing the affected scenes.\n\nThis window has layout issues: it allocates very little space to the list of affected scenes and too much space to the resource being deleted. Furthermore, these sections are not resizable; increasing the window height does not improve the visibility of the affected scenes.\n\nIn short, the area showing the affected scenes is too small and lacks the flexibility to be resized.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/YmH7FatLSgk\n\nThe screenshot shows a lot of dead space. None of the window sections allow for resizing to fill that area and increase the visible content. This empty space is currently wasted and cannot be utilized. I would like to expand the bottom panel where the file hierarchy is displayed, but it is currently locked/fixed and cannot be stretched.\n\n<img width=\"898\" height=\"1394\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b9b85aec-9bf4-43ab-b8fe-d75a80094a6e\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nsee the video\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n...","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"htt